          "source_text": "We often write <MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002>,\n<MATH_0003>, or <MATH_0004>\ninstead of the versions indexed by <MATH_0005>.\nUsing this notation, and using the description of\nlimits and colimits of sets in Section <REF_0001>\nbelow, we can say the following.\nLet <MATH_0006> be a diagram.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The object <MATH_0007> if it exists satisfies the following property\n<MATH_0008>\nwhere the limit on the right takes place in the category of sets.\n<STRUCT_0003> The object <MATH_0009> if it\nexists satisfies the following property\n<MATH_0010>\nwhere on the right we have the limit over the opposite category\nwith value in the category of sets.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nBy the Yoneda lemma (and its dual) this formula completely determines the\nlimit, respectively the colimit.\n",
          "source_text_hash": "sha256:51d40cfd0fb77378565a8d9d801da9475eb0c793eea4a5ec5dee1cfe7321b7e1",
